ed": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "PQ is parallel to SR in a trapezium PQRS. It is given that PQ > SR and the diagonals PR and QS intersect at O. If PO = 3 x − 15, OQ = x + 9, OR = x − 5 and OS = 5 and x has two values x1 and x2, then the value of (x12 - x22) is:", "options": [{"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "19", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "polygons", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "If the radius of a sphere is increased by 12 percent, then the volume will be increased by approximately:", "options": [{"text": "42.5 percent", "added": false}, {"text": "45.49 percent", "added": false}, {"text": "40.49 percent", "added": false}, {"text": "41.49 percent", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}]}